abstract: >-
  This lesson is designed for professionals in scholarly communication analytics, including researchers, 
  librarians, policy officers, and open science advocates, who work with open access (OA) publication data. 
  Participants will learn to enhance their technical skills in creating dashboards using open-source tools, 
  specifically Quarto. The lesson assumes basic computational skills, such as working with Markdown, dataframes, 
  and data visualization in Python or R, as well as a foundational understanding of the OA landscape. 
  By the end of the lesson, learners will be able to create and customize dashboards to track and visualize 
  OA metrics, supporting institutional reporting, compliance monitoring, and advocacy for open science.
